abstract: >
  Bayesian constraint pipeline for self-interacting dark matter (SIDM)
  cross-sections, with a feasibility survey of mediator detection.
  Combines WIMpy-style nested sampling (dynesty) with KiSS-SIDM
  gravothermal penalties, real LZ WS2024 + Fermi dwarf gamma-ray
  channels, and a composite-DM microphysics extension (dark glueballs,
  dark rho, dark baryons). Headline result: σ/m ~ 1-3 cm²/g at the
  MeV-mediator scale, with the mediator invisible to all direct-detection
  experiments (a ~10⁵⁰× margin below LZ) and decoupled from thermal-WIMP
  coupling by ~10⁰×. See docs/MATHEMATICS.md and the per-version
  synthesis docs in v0.3-prelim/docs/ for full derivation.
